From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:03:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 330/342] usb: print an invalid descriptor's length and
 configuration the right way round

"invalid descriptor length 0 in configuration 255" meant configuration 0
and a length of 255: the arguments were swapped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp
index fb4f8270f2..6b79e4b96c 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp
@@ -185,7 +185,7 @@ Device::Device(Object* parent, int8 hubAddress, uint8 hubPort,
 			if (descriptorLength < 2 || descriptorStart + descriptorLength > actualLength) {
 				TRACE_ERROR("invalid descriptor length %" B_PRIu8 " in configuration %" B_PRId32
 					", ignoring!\n",
-					i, descriptorLength);
+					descriptorLength, i);
 				break;
 			}
 
